      "keyInquiry": "How do plants exchange gases with their environment?",
      "purposeInStoryline": "In Lesson 1 students observed that bubbles emerged from specific spots on submerged sukuma wiki leaves, not uniformly across the entire surface. Lesson 2 gives the first layer of an answer: stomata are the openings most likely to let gas out at those spots (cut edges are another exit, which students meet again in Lesson 8). By naming, locating, and modelling these sites students gather the anatomical evidence needed to later explain why bubbles appear where they do, why temperature matters, and — ultimately — how plant respiration works at the cellular level.",
